course: dictionary
lesson: 592
title: Avalanche: a sudden rush
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An avalanche is a huge mass of snow, ice and rocks that suddenly slides fast down a mountain. Read the words around it to check. «The deadliest danger is a pyroclastic flow, an avalanche of hot gas, ash and rock racing downhill» tells you that an avalanche moves fast and downhill.
explain: Jess's room is a clue too. «An avalanche of socks, Lego and a mouldy apple fell on her» does not mean snow at all. It means a sudden, very large amount of things falling at once. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then swap in your meaning. "A sudden very large amount of socks, Lego and a mouldy apple fell on her" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Words can be used in a picture sense. Something that happens all at once, in a huge rush, can be called an avalanche. If an inbox is full of emails that arrive in one go, people call it an avalanche of emails. The real meaning, snow sliding fast, is the picture the word puts in your head.
fact: An avalanche is a huge mass of snow, ice and rocks that suddenly slides fast down a mountain.
fact: An avalanche of something means a sudden, very large amount of it.
fact: «Avalanche dogs find people buried in snow» by using their sense of smell.
fact: Skiers and climbers check avalanche warnings before they go onto steep slopes.
fact: Context clues, like «racing downhill» and «sudden», help you work out what avalanche means.
exercise: What is an avalanche? | *A huge mass of snow, ice and rocks sliding fast down a mountain | A tiny pile of soft snow in a garden | A warm wind that blows over a lake
exercise: In «an avalanche of socks, Lego and a mouldy apple fell on her», what does avalanche mean? | *A sudden, very large amount of things | A slow walk up the stairs | A cosy blanket
exercise: «The deadliest danger is a pyroclastic flow, an avalanche of hot gas, ash and rock racing downhill.» Which word tells you the avalanche moves fast? | ash | *racing | hot | calm
test: Why would a climber check avalanche warnings before going up a steep slope? | *To check the snow could slide down | To practise singing on the mountain | To find out whether snow might slide down | To see which café is open at the top
test: Ella says her inbox is an avalanche of emails. What does she mean? | *Far too many emails arrived all at once | She has been tidying her desk for hours | Her computer is covered in snow | The emails are cold and wet
exam: Mum says, «Your bedroom is an avalanche!» What does she mean? | Your bedroom has a window that opens slowly | *Your bedroom is in a sudden, huge mess of things | Your bedroom is covered in snow and rock | Your bedroom is a quiet, calm place
